SOAPBOX: I operated using wire antennas.  Due to Hurricane Dorian most local hams
SOAPBOX: were taking down antennas and our local W4MLB club station (Melbourne, FL)
SOAPBOX: cancelled a planned M/2 operation.  Most of our members live on the barrier
SOAPBOX: islands or within 10 Km of the Atlantic Ocean in the path of the hurricane.
SOAPBOX: Due to band conditions and wire antennas, I decided to operate high power.
SOAPBOX: Station:  ICOM IC-7300 with Ameritron AL-80B at 300 watts
SOAPBOX: Antennas: 20M = Delta Loop,  80/40/15 = Radio Works Super Loop
SOAPBOX: Logging:  N1MM+ and WSJT-X, which worked perfectly.  Thanks AA5AU for
SOAPBOX: excellent configuration instructions.
SOAPBOX: I worked both FT-4 (225 contacts) and FT-8 (82 contacts)
SOAPBOX: Thanks for the contacts es 73, Jan K4QD
